§§ `Occupational, congenital and genetic disease`

-- Bệnh nghề nghiệp: diseases characteristic of or related to an occupation, from regular and
-- long exposure to working conditions; the list is the one the Ministries of Health and of
-- Labour, Invalids and Social Affairs issue, which is outside the document. Bệnh / dị tật bẩm
-- sinh: formed in the foetus and present at birth. Bệnh Di truyền: passed down through genes,
-- determined by a doctor. Each is recorded on the claim as a condition the doctor names
-- (`an occupational disease`, `a congenital disease or defect`, `a genetic disease`); Part IV
-- items 14 and 17 read them.
